      "content": "The new EPA carbon emission mandates are mainly aimed at reducing greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions from industrial sources. As a small-scale metal fabrication business, you'll need to carefully measure and report your emissions, possibly invest in cleaner technologies or energy-efficient equipment, and may face financial penalties if your emissions exceed the mandated limits. Additionally, there might be opportunities for incentives or tax credits for implementing emissions-reducing measures. It's essential to accurately assess your current emissions and explore best practices to ensure compliance while maintaining profitability. Consultation with environmental experts and staying updated with EPA guidelines will also help in effectively managing the transition.",
